  "claude": {
    "enabled": true,
    "research": {
      "notes": "**1. Guidance**\n- I found no guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal inside 2026-09-15 to 2026-10-15.\n- Context from before the window: Rubrik reported Q2 FY27 on 2026-08-27 and raised all FY27 guided metrics. \nResults exceeded all guided metrics and guidance was raised for all FY27 metrics.\n — 2026-08-27 — https://ir.rubrik.com/news-events/press-releases/news-details/2026/Rubrik-Reports-Second-Quarter-Fiscal-Year-2027-Financial-Results/default.aspx\n- FY27 guidance after that raise: \nSubscription ARR of $1,880–1,885M, revenue of $1,685–1,693M and free cash flow of $323–333M.\n — 2026-08-27 — https://s203.q4cdn.com/667520861/files/content_files/Rubrik-Inc-99-1-Press-Release-7-31-2026-VFINAL.pdf\n- The Q1 FY27 guide, for comparison, was \nrevenue of $1.638–1.648B and free cash flow of $293–303M.\n — date unknown (Q1 report) — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/RBRK/8-k-rubrik-inc-reports-material-event-66cb05fbaed5.html\n- Results versus expectations: \nEPS was $0.20 against a $0.04 consensus. Revenue was $427.26M against a $396.30M consensus.\n — 2026-08-27 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NYSE/RBRK/earnings/\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- Wedbush initiated (assumed) coverage at Buy/Outperform with a $120 target. — 2026-10-09 — https://in.investing.com/equities/rubrik-consensus-estimates\n- Benzinga also lists the Wedbush assumption (Outperform, $120) but gives no date. — date unknown — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/RBRK/price-targets\n- I found no other rating or target changes inside the window. The post-earnings changes below were all on 2026-08-28, before the window:\n  - Citi: $96 to $130.\n  - DA Davidson: $90 to $115.\n  - Piper Sandler: $91 to $114.\n  - Guggenheim: $110 to $116.\n  - KeyBanc: $112 to $120.\n  - Sources: https://in.investing.com/equities/rubrik-consensus-estimates and https://tickernerd.com/stock/rbrk-forecast/\n- Consensus figures differ by source:\n  - \nMedian target of $120, range $110–139, from 28 analysts.\n — as of ~2026-10-07 — https://tickernerd.com/stock/rbrk-forecast/\n  - \nAverage target of $114.42, high $139, low $80, from 29 analysts.\n — date unknown — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NYSE/RBRK/forecast/\n\n**3. Litigation and regulation**\n- I found nothing material in the window.\n- Older suits (Commvault and Actifio patent cases, a 2020 DOJ probe of a former employee) turned up only in old coverage. I saw no new developments.\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- I found no customer wins or losses, and no concentration disclosures, in the window.\n- Background only: \nRubrik named its 2026 global partner award winners, including Ahead, Cognizant, Accenture, Arrow and CDW.\n — date unknown (blog dated ~June 2026) — https://www.rubrik.com/blog/company/26/6/congratulations-to-the-rubrik-2026-global-partner-award-winners\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- Sales continue under 10b5-1 plans, roughly monthly. The filings I saw don't state share counts, and the Form 4 URLs carry filing dates rather than trade dates.\n- A Form 4 was filed around 2026-10-02. The sale was under a plan \nadopted October 6, 2025\n, with \nweighted-average prices of $114.18–$115.16.\n Some shares are \nheld by the John and Sandra Thompson Trust, with the reporting person as co-trustee.\n — filing ~2026-10-02 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001943896/000120743326000022/form4-10022026_091056.xml\n- A Form 4 was filed around 2026-10-07. The sale was under a plan \nadopted October 15, 2025\n, at \nprices from $118.48 to $122.45.\n The reporting person isn't identified in the snippet. — filing ~2026-10-07 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001943896/000201914326000023/form4-10072026_101053.xml\n- Director Yvonne Wassenaar \nsold 721 shares on 2026-10-05, leaving 2,988 directly owned.\n — 2026-10-05 — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9112408/director-yvonne-wassenaar-sells-721-shares-of-rubrik-inc-rbrk (aggregator; I didn't find the original Form 4)\n- Earlier filings under the same two plans (Form 4 filings on 2026-09-04 and 2026-09-11) show the same pattern. The 09-04 filing is before the window; the 09-11 filing is also before it, though its trade dates are unknown. — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001943896/000120743326000020/form4-09042026_120923.xml and https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001943896/000201914326000019/form4-09112026_120951.xml\n- I found no insider purchases.\n\n**6. Product and competitive**\n- Rubrik announced a private preview of Code Guardian, which uses Anthropic's Claude Mythos 5 to red-team customer code from an air-gapped repository copy. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.rubrik.com/company/newsroom/press-releases/26/rubrik-unveils-code-guardian\n- \nCode Guardian and the new MCP access for AI agents are both private preview only.\n \nThe announcement gives no independent benchmarks, and the service isn't generally available.\n — 2026-09-16 — https://technode.global/2026/09/16/rubrik-code-guardian-mcp-agentic-cyber-resilience/\n- Rubrik added MCP support, and the release title says \n\"Rubrik AI Now Used by One Third of Global Customers.\"\n — 2026-09-16 — https://www.storagenewsletter.com/2026/09/22/rubrik-unveils-rubrik-code-guardian-harnessing-anthropics-claude-mythos-5-to-red-team-code-and-prioritize-cyber-risks/\n- Rubrik announced MSP program updates: \nbenefit tiers and consumption-based licensing.\n — date unknown — https://www.stocktitan.net/news/RBRK/rubrik-deepens-commitment-to-msp-operated-cyber-resilience-with-fhi2n6hrkvrt.html\n- Competitor: \nCohesity unveiled \"Agent Resilience\" for AI agent infrastructure protection.\n — date unknown (~mid-Sept 2026) — https://securitymea.com/2026/09/17/rubrik-unveils-code-guardian-for-air-gapped-code-red-teaming/\n- Before the window: the Q2 release shows \nGAAP gross margin of 78.4%, down from 79.5%, and non-GAAP gross margin of 81.0%, down from 81.6%.\n — 2026-08-27 — https://s203.q4cdn.com/667520861/files/content_files/Rubrik-Inc-99-1-Press-Release-7-31-2026-VFINAL.pdf\n- No pricing changes or share-gain data in the window.",
